<title>JAPAN: Tonen to cut staff, merge offices to lower costs.</title>
<headline>Tonen to cut staff, merge offices to lower costs.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Refiner Tonen Corp said on Tuesday it plans to reduce costs by a total of 26.5 billion yen by cutting its workforce and centralising offices by December 2000.</p>
<p>Tonen will reduce the number of staff at its headquarters and research centres by 250 employees to 450, saying the cost-cutting measures will allow the firm to remain competitive in Japan's post-deregulation oil market.</p>
<p>&quot;We need to achieve the target, no matter how difficult it is, to survive in the industry,&quot; a spokesman for Tonen said.</p>
</text>
